{
  "_why": "CANONICAL VOID PREDICATE per financial table (ACCT-F157). 'Exclude the voided row' had TEN different spellings across apps/backend/src (is_active=true 352, deleted_at IS NULL 285, voided_at IS NULL 269, soft_deleted_at IS NULL 199, archived_at IS NULL 150, revoked_at IS NULL 101, status<>'voided' 28, status NOT IN ('void') 11, reversed_by_je_id IS NULL 4, unapplied_at IS NULL 4). With no canonical predicate the invariant 'a money total never includes a voided row' cannot be guarded: every pattern either misses real defects or reddens on correct code. This map is the missing fact.",
  "_generated_from": "Neon prod br-fancy-credit-akjnd07a information_schema, 2026-08-07 (RLS-bypassed). Prod is authoritative over migrations.",
  "_precedence": "voided_at > soft_deleted_at > deleted_at > revoked_at > archived_at > unapplied_at > is_active. The strongest 'this did not happen' marker wins. is_active is LAST and canonical only when a table has nothing else, because on a transactional table it usually means enabled/disabled rather than voided \u2014 see _is_active_only below.",
  "_rules": [
    "A money aggregate over one of these tables MUST carry that table's predicate.",
    "A NEW financial table with a soft-delete column must be added here; verify-void-predicate-map-current.mjs fails otherwise.",
    "Never change a canonical_column to make a query pass \u2014 change the query."
  ],
  "_is_active_only": "Tables whose ONLY marker is is_active are mostly CONFIG/reference (banking_rules, chart_of_accounts_roles, escrow_settings, driver_pay_rates, transaction_categories, recurring_templates, expense_category_account_map). For those is_active means enabled, not voided. driver_finance.settlement_lines is the notable EXCEPTION: it is transactional money and is_active IS its void marker (ACCT-F156 fixed two aggregates that omitted it).",
